Load the OpenCL ICD loader by its runtime SONAME.

Debian and Ubuntu only ship the unversioned libOpenCL.so in their -dev
packages, so without this MNN finds no OpenCL on a normal desktop install.

--- a/source/backend/opencl/core/runtime/OpenCLWrapper.cpp
+++ b/source/backend/opencl/core/runtime/OpenCLWrapper.cpp
@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@
         "/system/vendor/lib/libPVROCL.so", "/data/data/org.pocl.libs/files/lib/libpocl.so"
 #endif
 #elif defined(__linux__)
+        "libOpenCL.so.1",
         "/usr/lib/libOpenCL.so",
         "/usr/local/lib/libOpenCL.so",
         "/usr/local/lib/libpocl.so",
